{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Ruby missing: no install step before ruby -v",
    "Explanation": [
      "The step list shows only 'Spin up environment', 'Preparing environment variables', 'Checkout code', and then 'ruby -v'. No step ran before 'ruby -v' that tried to install Ruby. The config also shows the 'Add step below to install Ruby version 2.6.3' slot left empty and the orbs section holding only a placeholder comment. That is why the job failed with 'ruby: command not found' (exit code 127).",
      "",
      "The requirement keeps cimg/base:stable as the executor, which rules out changing the base image. Increasing the timeout does nothing, because the failure is a missing binary, not a time limit. Installing via apt does not reliably give Ruby 2.6.3 exactly, since distro packages ship whatever version that release carries.",
      "",
      "The config's own placeholders ('# Add Orb here' and the empty install-step slot) point to the intended fix. Declare the CircleCI Ruby orb (circleci/ruby) under orbs, then add its install step before 'ruby -v', for example 'ruby/install: version: \"2.6.3\"'. This provides that exact version inside the config without touching the image. The artifacts themselves do not show the orb's command syntax, so that snippet comes from general knowledge of the orb rather than the frozen files."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"fix\": \"add_ruby_orb\",",
      "  \"install_attempted\": false",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"fix\": \"add_ruby_orb\",",
        "  \"install_attempted\": false",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
