{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy ran on non-production branch",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow run summary shows build-test-and-deploy finished SUCCESS, with all three jobs green, so the pipeline was green. However, the run was on branch `koans-08-branch-filters`, not `production`, and the `deploy` job still ran and executed `echo \"Deploy complete\"`. This violates the requirement that deploy run only for commits to `production`, so the behaviour was incorrect. The config has no branch filters at all; deploy is gated only by `requires: [test-production]`, which controls ordering, not branches. The fix belongs on the `deploy` entry under `workflows.build-test-and-deploy.jobs`, adding `filters: branches: only: production`. Branch filters are not valid on the job definition under `jobs:`, and an ignore-list cannot reliably exclude every possible non-production branch. Since build and test-production have no branch restriction, they still run on production, so the workflow stays green there."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_branches_only_production\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
