{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy runs on untagged push; needs beta tag filters on all jobs",
    "Explanation": [
      "pipeline_green: The workflow summary shows `build-test-and-deploy` finished with SUCCESS, and build, test and deploy all succeeded, so the run was green.",
      "",
      "behaviour_correct: The run came from an API trigger on branch `koans-09-tag-filters`, and no tag appears in the artifacts. The `deploy` job has no filters, so it ran and deployed on an untagged branch push. The requirement forbids this, so the behaviour was incorrect.",
      "",
      "fix_target_job: In CircleCI, jobs do not run for tag pushes unless they have an explicit `tags` filter. CircleCI also requires tag filters on every job that a tag-triggered job depends on, directly or indirectly. `deploy` requires `test`, which requires `build`. Adding a tag filter only to `deploy` would leave `build` and `test` skipped when `beta-main-0.1.1` is pushed, so `deploy` could never run. All three jobs therefore need tag filters in the workflow.",
      "",
      "fix: The chosen change is a beta-only tag filter (`tags: only: /^beta-.*/`), applied across the dependency chain. `deploy` must also have `branches: ignore: /.*/` so that untagged branch pushes do not deploy. With this, `beta-main-0.1.1` and `beta-secondary-0.1.1` produce a green workflow that deploys. `alpha-*` tags and untagged branch pushes do not deploy.",
      "",
      "Caveat: the fix options only partly fit. 'filters_tags_only_beta' describes the tag filter, and the required `branches: ignore` on `deploy` is part of this fix rather than a separate option."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
